## Former audit findings, side by side with the implementation

### A1 — trusted free-trial identity and guest authority: COMPLETE

The deployed two-application path now has one login form in the room. The room sends the submitted credentials to the controller's authoritative entry decision and persists `decision.asFreeTrial` on the server session. Every later request and realtime roster frame reads the session-owned value, so trial chat, PM, badge, random-selection, and app-delivery gates receive the same fact.

The final audit also found and closed a privilege-escalation edge: a signed `guest` token carried a self-declared email and could previously trigger a membership lookup. `authorityEmailForHandoff` now licenses membership lookup only for an authenticated `site` handoff; guest and absent handoffs resolve with no membership authority.

