### A2 — alert delivery and reporting: COMPLETE for the supported FCM channel

Alert creation and scheduling now transactionally enqueue delivery work. The room owns a durable SQLite outbox with stale-claim recovery, bounded retry timing, and stable idempotency keys. The controller owns PostgreSQL dispatch, recipient-attempt, and cross-room-link ledgers. The worker applies member eligibility and `freeTrialsGetApp`, sends through FCM, records terminal outcomes/timestamps/reasons, and prunes registrations only on provider-confirmed dead-token classifications.

The send boundary now re-reads and enforces every repository-held authority fact before talking to FCM: the room-wide `diasableFCMAlerts` kill switch, current membership/invite state, pause/unsubscribe state, `alerterAppFcmUserOff`, free-trial and case-by-case app policy, marketplace subscription state/current paid period, and `mobileAppExpireNotificationsDays` as the final login-age backstop. Marketplace states other than `active` or `trialing` fail closed. A missing login timestamp also fails closed while decay is enabled. This closes the paired-phone cancellation leak without deleting registrations; only FCM's provider-confirmed `UNREGISTERED` result licenses pruning.

Presenter reports query real persisted attempts; they support recipient/status filtering, linked-room identity, timestamps, reasons, registration counts, and pruned-token counts. The UI no longer fabricates an empty report.

`linkedRoomAlerts` is limited to same-account targets, excludes the source room, deduplicates, caps fan-out at 20, creates idempotently linked dispatches, and aggregates their results into the source report. `dontCrossPost` is validated, stored in immediate and scheduled alerts, retained across outbox retries, included in the controller's immutable idempotency input, and suppresses linked fan-out.

The supported external channel is FCM push. SMS, email, and social-provider flags that have no configured, governed sender are rejected rather than accepted and silently discarded. Provider credentials are not sent to the browser.

