### A3 — recordings/archive product: COMPLETE

The first-party browser recorder now finalizes and uploads its media automatically. Uploads stream to a temporary file, enforce authentication/authorization and size/type limits, compute SHA-256 during ingestion, and publish by atomic rename only after success. The archive has a durable catalog plus immutable log snapshots for chat, alerts, and transcript context.

Authorized members can page the room archive, play/download with HTTP range requests, and download the captured transcript. Presenters can delete catalog and media atomically at the product boundary. `recsInRoom` gates the room tab and the archive entitlement is enforced again on list and media routes; UI hiding is never the authority.

