### A6 — immediate permission refresh: COMPLETE

After the controller commits a permission change, the room publishes one addressed `forceReload` command to the target user. The client reloads its server-derived session/config state. No success command is published if the controller write fails, so downgrades cannot be acknowledged before authority changes.

Evidence: `apps/room/src/routes/permissions.remote.ts`, `apps/room/src/routes/sess/[room]/events/+server.ts`, and `apps/room/src/lib/permission-refresh-contract.test.ts`.

### A7 — public anonymous stream player: COMPLETE

A presenter can enable, inspect, copy, and revoke a public-player grant. The raw grant is returned once; only its SHA-256 digest is stored. Grants are room-scoped, expiring, and revocable. The public route exchanges a valid grant for a five-minute read-only media token and sends `private, no-store`. The player contains screenshare HLS only—no chat, notes, files, roster, private messages, or publishing credential.

